   - Explicit ""8 Begründungen"" section explaining design choices (✗ model lacks this)
   
   The model's release notes are excellent but don't include the meta-commentary on why certain decisions were made.

5. **Commit-to-Release-Notes mapping table** – The golden standard includes a detailed table showing how each commit was transformed (Commit → Problem → User-Facing Solution). The model has this in section 4 but it's less detailed than the golden standard's mapping.

6. **Deprecated section handling** – The model includes a ""⚠️ Deprecated"" section with v1 endpoints, but the golden standard treats this as part of ""Breaking Changes"" with more emphasis. The distinction is minor but affects clarity.

