   - Golden standard: ""~99%"" with more nuanced discussion of assumptions and their impact on real-world applicability

5. **Additional Insights:**
   - The golden standard explains why intuition fails (253 pairs vs. linear thinking)
   - The golden standard discusses how real-world data (non-uniform births) affects the result
   - The model response is more straightforward but less insightful

## Quality Assessment

**Strengths of Model Response:**
- Exceptionally clear and well-organized
- Excellent pedagogical structure with numbered steps
- Thorough explanation of the complementary approach
- Correct mathematics throughout
- Appropriate confidence level with reasoning
- Good use of formatting and tables

**Weaknesses Relative to Golden Standard:**
- Lacks discussion of numerical stability/logarithmic calculation
- Doesn't explain the combinatorial intuition (253 pairs)
- Doesn't discuss how real-world deviations from assumptions affect results
- Confidence stated as 100% rather than acknowledging limitations of assumptions
- Less sophisticated mathematical presentation

## Standard Adherence

