- Golden standard is more minimalist and measured (""Kein Blabla, keine halben Sachen"")
- Model uses ""graben so lange"" (dig until we understand) vs. golden's ""denken Dinge neu"" (rethink things)
- Model's ""Punkt"" vs. golden's ""Versprochen"" – both work, different emphasis (finality vs. commitment)

The model's text is **slightly more aggressive/emphatic** than the golden standard, which is more understated. Both are valid Berlin agency tones, but the golden standard's restraint is arguably more sophisticated for the target audience.

## Standard Adherence

