2. Mathematical quantification of the deficit
3. Depth of reasoning and justification
4. Completeness of alternatives (3 vs. 4 options)
5. Provision of a concrete example schedule

The model is **good but not excellent**. It solves the problem correctly but with less depth and formality than the golden standard. A user would find it helpful, but a senior evaluator would note the lack of structured reasoning and comprehensive justification.

**Score: 4 (Good)**

